  "guide": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "title": "Your desk, in one place",
      "body": "Your business answers are saved here. The checklist shows what is complete and what needs attention. Website chat, phone and texting have separate statuses, so you can see exactly what customers can use.",
      "action": "See my setup"
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "title": "Make the answers yours",
      "body": "Open What it knows and check your services, service area, published prices, hours and safety instructions. Save any corrections, then select “I reviewed these saved rules.” Changes require another review and test.",
      "action": "Review my rules"
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "title": "Practice the requests you get",
      "body": "Try a customer booking, callback request or question in Test it. The result shows the details collected. Practice does not book a real visit, contact anyone, use your actual capacity or change a calendar.",
      "action": "Try a private conversation"
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "title": "Protect time you have already booked",
      "body": "Under Availability, block a whole day or an arrival window for existing jobs, closures or time off. Existing visits stay booked. Calendar sync is not connected, so keep outside work up to date here.",
      "action": "Check availability"
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "title": "Choose when customers can use it",
      "body": "Setup lists the requirements for website chat. When the saved rules have been reviewed and tested with the working AI service, activate chat and install the code on your website. Phone and text messages stay inactive until their own setup is verified.",
      "action": "See activation and installation"
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "title": "Know what needs you each day",
      "body": "Leads and bookings holds customer requests; Conversations shows what was said. Check these regularly while phone and text alerts are inactive. Pause website chat from the top of this page, export your records under Account, and reopen this guide whenever you need it.",
      "action": "View customer requests"
    }
  ],
